WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.820
The Kurds live across the border area spanning
Iran, Iraq, Turkey, and Syria.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.040
They say that they're the largest people today
without a nation, and that may very well be

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.040
true.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.470
They thought that they could have a country
in the wake of World War I, but at the end,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:24.369
it was denied to them by the great powers,
by oil interests, and so forth.

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:29.000
In recent decades, the Kurds have suffered
tremendous oppression under a variety of dictators,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.210
especially in Iraq where Saddam Hussein famously
used chemical weapons against them.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:39.600
They've also led a bloody, bloody insurgency
in Turkey, a group that's called the PKK or

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.590
the Kurdistan Workers Party.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:47.530
That insurgency has claimed the lives of more
than 40,000 people between 1984 and the present,

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.140
and we've recently seen an upswing of violence
there.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.530
The important thing to remember about the
Kurds, however, is while they claim that they're

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.359
one people, in reality, they're divided among
many, many different political groups.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:05.790
And often times, they spend just as much time
fighting each other as fighting others.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.360
Is there room for another nation-state in
the Middle East?

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.330
Should we be in the business of redrawing
borders?

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.910
Let us know in the comments, and let us know
what other topics you want us to cover in

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.850
sixty seconds.

